      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hello! I also thought about that and perfectly agree. In fact this function already gets DBus parameters (service, path, ifact), so it can query the rest by itself. So, i would encapsulate SPI parameters into a struct, like:\n  \nstruct SPIDevParams\n{\n    uint64_t spiControllerIndex;\n    uint64_t spiDeviceIndex;\n\n};\n\n  \nAnd implement one function, like getSPIParameters(service, path, configIface) which fills it in. This would also get rid of unused params in createBIOSDevice(). So the device creation code would look like:\n\nstatic sdbusplus::async::task\u003cstd::unique_ptr\u003cSPIDevice\u003e\u003e createBIOSDevice(\n    sdbusplus::async::context\u0026 ctx\u003e, bool dryRun, GPIOGroup\u0026\u0026 muxGPIO,\n    SoftwareConfig\u0026 config,\n    SoftwareManager* parent, const std::string\u0026 service,\n    const sdbusplus::object_path\u0026 path, const std::string\u0026 configIFace)\n{\n    auto spi_params \u003d co_await getSPIDevParameters(service, path, configIFace);\n\n    co_return std::make_unique\u003cBIOSDevice\u003e(\n        ctx, spi_params, dryRun, names, values, config,\n        parent);\n}\n\nstatic sdbusplus::async::task\u003cstd::unique_ptr\u003cSPIDevice\u003e\u003e createMyFancyVendorSpecificDevice(\n    sdbusplus::async::context\u0026 ctx\u003e, bool dryRun, GPIOGroup\u0026\u0026 muxGPIO,\n    SoftwareConfig\u0026 config,\n    SoftwareManager* parent, const std::string\u0026 service,\n    const sdbusplus::object_path\u0026 path, const std::string\u0026 configIFace)\n{\n    auto spi_params \u003d co_await getSPIDevParameters(service, path, configIFace);\n    auto my_extra_params \u003d co_await getMyFancyParameters(service, path, configIFace);\n  \n    co_return std::make_unique\u003cMyVendorSpecificDevice\u003e(\n        ctx, spi_params, extra_params, dryRun, muxGPIO, config,\n        parent);\n}\n\nWould such design be okay for you ?",
